<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jamil Mahuad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1949">1949</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jamil Mahuad was mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> and president of Ecuador from 1998 to 2000. He signed the peace agreement of 1998 that ended the border dispute with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, but his government faced a severe banking collapse and froze bank deposits in 1999. In January 2000 he announced the adoption of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> dollar and was overthrown days later by indigenous protesters and army officers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jamil-mahuad.jpg" alt="Jamil Mahuad" width="320" height="364" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pedroparker04 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamil_Mahuad_01_corte.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
